            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-24791-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-24791 high vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The net/http HTTP/1.1 client mishandled the case where a server responds to a request with an \"Expect: 100-continue\" header with a non-informational (200 or higher) status. This mishandling could leave a client connection in an invalid state, where the next request sent on the connection will fail. An attacker sending a request to a net/http/httputil.ReverseProxy proxy can exploit this mishandling to cause a denial of service by sending \"Expect: 100-continue\" requests which elicit a non-informational response from the backend. Each such request leaves the proxy with an invalid connection, and causes one subsequent request using that connection to fail."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-24791\nSeverity: high\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.17.7\nFix Version: 1.21.12,1.22.5\nType: go-module\nLocation: /opt/cni/bin/istio-cni\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2024-24791](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-24791)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-24791**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | stdlib  | go1.17.7  | 1.21.12,1.22.5  | go-module  | /opt/cni/bin/istio-cni  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2024-24791](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-24791)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.17.7"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-24785-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-24785 medium vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "If errors returned from MarshalJSON methods contain user controlled data, they may be used to break the contextual auto-escaping behavior of the html/template package, allowing for subsequent actions to inject unexpected content into templates."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-24785\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.17.7\nFix Version: 1.21.8,1.22.1\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/install-cni\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2024-24785](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-24785)",
